   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The Spanish of the screen",
     "texto": [
      "**The device.** The ordenador (in Latin America, la computadora) has a **pantalla**, a **teclado** and a **ratón**. An **archivo** lives in a **carpeta**.\n\n**What you do.** You **pinchas en** a **enlace**, **arrastras** a file into a folder, **configuras** a program and **actualizas** the system. To log in you need a **contraseña**.\n\n**Problems.** If the computer **se bloquea**, you **reinicias** it. To lose nothing, you make a **copia de seguridad**.\n\n**By accident.** When something happens by accident, we use **se + me/te/le**: **Se me ha borrado el archivo.** The verb agrees with what gets deleted: **Se me han borrado las fotos.**\n\n**Instructions with usted.** The technician gives orders: **Pinche**, **mantenga**, **reinicie**. With **hasta que** and the future, the verb goes in the subjunctive."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "By accident and with usted",
     "texto": [
      "**Se + me/te/le + verb** tells something that happens by accident. The person affected goes in **me, te, le, nos, os, les**; the verb agrees with what happens: **Se me ha borrado el archivo. Se me han borrado las fotos.**\n\n**Formal commands.** The present subjunctive is used: **Pinche**, **mantenga**, **reinicie**. Verbs in **-ar** end in **-e**; verbs in **-er** and **-ir**, in **-a**: **escriba**, **abra**.\n\n**Hasta que + subjunctive** when you talk about the future: **Espere hasta que se cargue la página.**"
     ],
